+# Held Reservation Resolution Act — reviewable technical candidate (2026-11-25)
+
+Status: **candidate implementation and isolated tests only.** The bill
+`records/bills/held-reservation-resolution-act.md` is a DRAFT and is **not
+enacted**. Nothing here is deployed, proposed for delivery, merged, activated or
+claimed as a repair of the live foresight lockout. Work is confined to worktree
+branch `executive/held-reservation-candidate-20261125` (base `d8c906cb`).
+
+## Authority and semantics review (stop condition checked)
+
+No conflict with enacted law or existing safety semantics was found that would
+require stopping before implementation. The draft's narrow resolution path is
+consistent with the fail-closed rules, provided one accounting floor is applied:
+
+- Act 32 §3 / amendment H: unknown meter state blocks dispatch — preserved. The
+  new path closes only on independently attested terminal identity plus a
+  readable, validly bounded meter; every other path tightens the hold at full
+  cap (`/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche/government/LAWS.md` lines 489–760).
+- Act 33 §3 and Act 34 §3(2), §4(1): the cumulative UPPER_BOUND liability is
+  non-resettable and never reduced by restart/rename/re-permit (LAWS.md lines
+  762–776, 808, 875). `knowledge-budget-tool.py` `charges()` charges a **closed**
+  row from `.usage`, not `.charge` (tool line 311). Therefore the candidate
+  floors `.usage` at every cap **and** the prior `.charge` on each dimension;
+  otherwise closure with a small real meter reading would have reduced the held
+  liability. `retain_overrun_floor` and monotone `merge_usage_snapshots` are
+  retained. This is a preservation requirement, not a relaxation.
+- Act 34 §4(3) (ledger/stop-hold semantics) and §4(4) (enforcement bytes): a
+  real deployment of this behaviour needs a Parliament law change, Executive
+  permit terms, Economy re-verification and independent verification of the
+  exact bytes (LAWS.md lines 879–881). This candidate performs none of those.
+- Act 32 §9 activation gate and draft §5: closing the reservation removes only
+  the budget blocker; `guard` still applies all existing admission checks and
+  a fresh appointment still needs new independent instructions. No replay or
+  live-session rebind is implemented.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `government/knowledge-budget.sh`: added a **separate** guarded subcommand
+  `resolve-session RESERVATION_ID REASON --session SID --by OPERATOR` and its
+  locked worker `resolve_session_locked()`. It operates only on `state=held`,
+  uses the existing flock/atomic-write/res_write conventions, and changes no
+  other subcommand. The command itself re-reads `antonina agent status` for the
+  row's exact non-empty agent and requires a non-empty native session id equal
+  to `SID` and a terminal state (`clearexit|failed|stopped|killed`); unreadable or
+  malformed status, agent-id mismatch, SID mismatch/missing, non-terminal agent,
+  empty row agent id, absent resolver and absent SID all stay held with a
+  recorded reason via `tighten_held_locked`. A bound row whose stored native
+  session differs from `SID` is also held (no cross-session metering). On a
+  passing attestation an unreadable meter or invalid/reset CPU bound keeps the
+  full-cap hold; a valid snapshot is merged monotonically, floored as above and
+  applied to `retain_overrun_floor`. Closure writes `closed_reason =
+  operator_resolved_session:<REASON>`, `resolved_by`, a `resolution_attestation`
+  (SID, agent, terminal state, resolver, reason, timestamp, status source),
+  appends history and calls `refresh_aggregate`. No agent kill/stop, run, replay
+  or hand ledger edit. POSIX `/bin/sh`, no bashisms (`/bin/sh -n` clean).
+- `tests/held-reservation-resolve-session-smoke.sh`: new isolated adversarial
+  suite (scratch state, PATH-first antonina stub, no live credentials or
+  `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/knowledge/budget` access).
+
+## Verification (from this worktree, via canonical suite-env)
+
+- `/bin/sh /var/lib/lubko/wd/viche/government/suite-env.sh /bin/sh tests/held-reservation-resolve-session-smoke.sh`
+  → PASS. Covers: valid null-session closure with attestation, provenance and
+  monotone charge and unchanged aggregate; `guard foresight` flip to ok only
+  after valid closure; unreadable/malformed status, SID mismatch, non-terminal,
+  wrong agent, empty row agent, absent/empty SID, absent resolver; missing
+  meter; reset/invalid CPU bound; above-cap charge never reduced; all four
+  terminal states; no cross-session rebind; existing `resolve` unchanged;
+  non-held row refused; concurrent resolves close exactly once under flock;
+  no reported cost → `cost_reported=false`; no kill/stop or new reservation
+  (no replay); unrelated office reservation byte-identical and still guarded.
+- `suite-env.sh /bin/sh tests/knowledge-budget-smoke.sh` → PASS.
+- `suite-env.sh /bin/sh tests/knowledge-budget-finalize-after-stop-smoke.sh`
+  → PASS (T1–T19).
+- `suite-env.sh /bin/sh tests/knowledge-budget-negative-20261122.sh` → T1–T7
+  PASS; **T8 fails because the shipped config has all offices `enabled: true`**.
+  Verified on a pristine `git archive HEAD` copy: the same T8 failure is
+  pre-existing and unrelated to this candidate. No full suite was run here;
+  the exact-candidate full suite is the integration gate.
+
+## Limitations / open obligations
+
+- Not law, not deployed, not reviewed by an independent party. No claim that
+  foresight is repaired; the live held row `r1795595445-NZIjZE34` was not read
+  or touched.
+- A fresh foresight appointment with new instructions and the no-replay
+  acceptance item require lawful Executive action after enactment; they are
+  outside this code candidate and are not asserted here.
+- The trust boundary is the `antonina agent status` instrument; the command
+  re-reads it but cannot independently prove the runtime's integrity.
+- The pre-existing `knowledge-budget-negative-20261122.sh` T8 config mismatch
+  is left unchanged (out of scope); it should be tracked separately.
+
+No production ledger, activation, permit, attestation, board, budget state,
+credential, live agent or external side effect was created, edited or replayed
+by this work.
